    native_engine2d_runtime_queue_symbols_2026-06-14, 1, "2026-11-13: Correction to the 2026-11-11 verdict, source read at release/1.0.0 5221a5058a8, Linux aarch64 (DGX Spark GB10), Rust seed af717f53d6bce3e5, nothing run: the CPU-only import split described there is not in the tree. draw_ir_runtime_queue_spec.spl still imports std.gc_async_mut.gpu.engine2d.engine.{Engine2D}, and so does draw_ir_runtime_adv.spl, so the spec closure still pulls the CUDA/Vulkan backends. The rt_host_gpu_queue_* definitions exist in src/runtime/runtime_native.c; their presence in a linked ELF binary was not checked on this host (the nm evidence is Windows-only)."

